  "title": "Connecting and Breaking the Ice",
  "summary": "Paul percebe um jovem viajante cansado em uma praça, aproxima-se com gentileza e pratica uma escuta atenta para ajudá-lo com seu fardo emocional.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/great-commission-01.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "Paul sits in a quiet public square and notices a tired young man holding his head in his hands. Sensing his quiet struggle, Paul decides to approach him with a calm smile.\n\n“Good afternoon,” Paul says softly. “May I sit beside you?”\n\nThe man looks up, surprised by such genuine kindness. “Sure,” he replies with a sigh.\n\nPaul chooses an attitude of deep empathy. Instead of giving quick answers, he practices patient listening as the stranger begins to share his story. The man speaks about the heavy burden he carries in his daily life and the loneliness he feels in the crowded city.\n\nWith gentle encouragement, Paul speaks words of hope. “You do not have to walk through this alone,” Paul says warmly. The stranger smiles for the first time, feeling understood and supported.",
